.TH CTI-SUPPLIER 1 "2026-11-08" "cti-agent 1.6" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-supplier \- supplier-request lane: find new supplier requests, judge them, file Kanban items, write the digest
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti-supplier
.RB ( \-\-dry\-run | \-\-for\-real )
.B \-\-collect
.I DIR
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR DURATION ]
.PP
.B cti-supplier
.RB ( \-\-dry\-run | \-\-for\-real )
.B \-\-finish
.I DIR
.PP
.B cti-supplier \-\-for\-real \-\-commit\-seen
.I FILE
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-supplier
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-supplier
is the deterministic half of the supplier-request lane;
.BR run\-supplier (1)
drives it and the model between its two stages. It sends no mail. It changes
nothing in the mailbox, never replies to a requester, and never opens the tax or
bank attachments.
.PP
Like every command that files or records something, it must be told how to run:
.B \-\-dry\-run
reads and judges and writes only its own work directory;
.B \-\-for\-real
also files the Kanban items and records what was reported. With neither it prints
usage and exits 2.
.SS \-\-collect
Reads the CTI mailbox (Graph, read-only) for messages received in the window
that have
.B SUPPLIER_ADDRESS
in To or Cc, groups them into conversations (one request each), and skips the
fleet's own mail and any request already reported. For each it reads the
supplier request form from an attached
.B .xlsx
(fields are found by their label text, not their position; blanks stay blank;
required fields left empty are listed), and records whether the form was
.BR read ,
.B linked
(shared as a link in the message, which is not opened),
.B unreadable
(a spreadsheet that is not the form) or
.B none
(judged from the message text). It writes
.B requests.json
and one
.B NNN.input.txt
per request, in which the request sits inside an untrusted block. The only way
code reaches attachment bytes is a policy that opens
.B .xlsx
files only, refuses names that contain a whole word such as w9, bank, routing,
void, tax, irs or ach, and caps the size.
.SS \-\-finish
Reads each
.B NNN.result.json
the runner saved from the model. A request with none is Unsure. Every answer is
checked: quotes must be copied from the request, a No is refused where the form
was not read or the name or notes hold a technology word or the request tried to
steer the reader, and output that cannot be parsed is Unsure. Code only ever
moves an answer toward Unsure.
.PP
A Yes or an Unsure needs a Kanban item. With
.B \-\-for\-real
it is found by its label (one per conversation, so a rerun never files twice) or
filed in
.BR SUPPLIER_JIRA_PROJECT ,
which must be in
.BR JIRA_ALLOW_CREATE .
The item carries the business fields of the form and the reason, and no address,
contact or remittance detail. A failure to file one item is recorded and does not
stop the others or the digest, and a request that failed is not recorded as
reported, so the next run tries again.
.PP
A request reported before is judged again when its thread has a newer message.
If the verdict changed, or the form is now read, a comment is added to its
existing item saying what changed; if nothing changed it is quiet. The lane never
closes, reopens or edits an item. Each Yes or Unsure item lists what is still
needed (the form, blank required fields, what the supplier will provide), in
fixed wording, since the lane never contacts the requester. Writes
.BR digest.html ,
.BR digest.txt ,
.BR digest.subject ,
.B seen.json
and
.BR problems.txt .
.SS \-\-commit\-seen
Records the requests in a
.B seen.json
as reported, in
.BR state/supplier\-seen.json ,
which holds, per request, a label, dates, the verdict and the Kanban item's key, and no supplier name or request text. Run by
.BR run\-supplier (1)
after a real send.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Read and judge, say what would be filed, write nothing to Jira or the record of what was reported.
.TP
.B \-\-for\-real
With \-\-finish, file the Kanban items. With \-\-commit\-seen, record the requests as reported.
.TP
.BI \-\-collect " DIR"
Find new supplier requests and write what the model needs into this directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-finish " DIR"
Judge the requests in this directory, file the items and write the digest.
.TP
.BI \-\-commit\-seen " FILE"
Record a seen.json so the same requests are not reported again, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-since " DURATION"
How far back to look for requests (default
.B SUPPLIER_WINDOW_DAYS
days, else 3).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
See
.BR run\-supplier (1)
for the SUPPLIER_* settings. Jira uses JIRA_BASE_URL, JIRA_EMAIL, JIRA_API_TOKEN, JIRA_CLOUD_ID and JIRA_ALLOW_CREATE; Graph uses TENANT_ID, CLIENT_ID, CLIENT_SECRET, GRAPH_MAILBOX and GRAPH_FOLDER.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The stage finished.
.TP
.B 1
The mailbox could not be read, a file could not be written, or a setting is invalid.
.TP
.B 2
No mode was given, or the modes contradict each other.
.SH EXAMPLES
Look for requests and see what the model would be shown:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-supplier \-\-dry\-run \-\-collect /tmp/supplier\-work
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-supplier (1),
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
.BR cti\-jira (1)
